.TH HOMELAB-API 8 "2026-07-31" "homelab-api" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
homelab-api \- Homelab Drive JSON API server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B homelab-api
.br
(started via
.B hypnotoad
under the
.B homelab-api.service
systemd unit; not normally invoked directly)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B homelab-api
is the JSON API backend for the Homelab Drive file storage service. It
handles user authentication (JWT issuance/refresh against a
.I dovecot.users
table), Drive file/directory CRUD, sharing, and enqueues asynchronous
work (thumbnail and slideshow-image generation, copy/move processing)
for
.BR homelab-api-backend-processor (8)
to pick up.
.P
It runs as a Mojolicious application under Hypnotoad and is managed via
systemd; it is not intended to be run interactively.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/homelab/api/config.yml
Main configuration file (YAML). See CONFIGURATION below.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOMELAB_API_CONFIG
Overrides the path to the configuration file (default
.IR /etc/homelab/api/config.yml ).
Set by the shipped systemd unit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is YAML with the following top-level sections.
.SS database
PostgreSQL connection used for both the
.I api
schema (Drive data) and read-only
.I dovecot.users
lookups (login).
.TP
.B host
Database host or IP (e.g. a pgbouncer endpoint). No default \- required.
.TP
.B port
Database port. Default:
.IR 5432 .
.TP
.B name
Database name. Default:
.IR mailserver .
.TP
.B user
Database role. Default:
.IR homelab_api .
Should be a dedicated least-privilege role: CRUD on
.I api.*
plus read-only
.I SELECT
on
.IR dovecot.users .
.TP
.B password
Database password for
.BR user .
No default \- required.
.SS jwt
.TP
.B secret
Signing key for issued JWTs. No default \- required; use a long random
value in production.
.TP
.B algorithm
JWT signing algorithm. Default:
.IR HS256 .
.TP
.B expiry_seconds
Access token lifetime, in seconds. Default:
.I 3600
(1 hour).
.TP
.B refresh_expiry_seconds
Refresh token lifetime, in seconds. Default:
.I 2592000
(30 days).
.SS session
.TP
.B secure
Boolean (0/1). When set, marks session/auth cookies
.BR Secure ;
set to
.I 1
when served behind an HTTPS-terminating proxy, otherwise
.IR 0 .
Default:
.IR 0 .
.SS server
Hypnotoad listen/worker configuration.
.TP
.B host
Bind address, or a full
.I http://
URL (in which case
.B port
below is ignored). Default:
.IR 0.0.0.0 .
.TP
.B port
Bind port (ignored if
.B host
is a full URL). Default:
.IR 3000 .
.TP
.B workers
Number of Hypnotoad worker processes. Default:
.I 2
in code; the shipped example config sets
.IR 4 .
.TP
.B heartbeat_timeout
Seconds before Hypnotoad kills a worker that has stopped responding to
heartbeats. Hypnotoad's own built-in default is
.I 50
seconds; the shipped example config raises this to
.I 600
to accommodate large uploads. Only applied if set.
.TP
.B accepts
Optional: passed through as Hypnotoad's
.I accepts
worker setting (requests handled before a worker recycles). Unset by
default (Hypnotoad's own default applies).
.TP
.B max_clients
Optional: passed through as Hypnotoad's
.I clients
worker setting (max concurrent connections per worker). Unset by
default (Hypnotoad's own default applies).
.SS logging
.TP
.B level
Log verbosity (e.g.
.IR debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error ).
Default:
.IR info .
.TP
.B format
Log line format,
.I json
or plain text. Default:
.IR json .
.SS storage
.TP
.B drive_path
Filesystem path (typically an NFS mount) where Drive file content and
derivatives are stored.
.B homelab-api-backend-processor
must be configured with the identical path, since it accesses the same
mount independently.
.TP
.B max_file_size_mb
Per-upload hard size limit, in megabytes. Default:
.I 10240
(10GB).
.TP
.B max_concurrent_uploads
Concurrency limit advertised to clients. Default:
.IR 4 .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR homelab-api-backend-processor (8),
.BR homelab-drive-web-ui (8)
.P
Full example configuration:
.I /usr/share/doc/homelab-api/config.example.yml
.SH BUGS
Changing
.B database
credentials requires restarting the service
.RI ( "systemctl restart homelab-api" )
\- configuration is only read at startup.
